{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>To the heads of the tribes.</b> In order to compel the people. One may say: this pericope was stated after the war against Midian, for the pericopes are contiguous up to 'and whatever proceeds from your mouth you shall do' — therefore the pericope of Mattot, in which is written 'whatever proceeds from his mouth he shall do,' was juxtaposed to it. Rashi explained: and from where do we know that all the other commandments are likewise [taught to all Israel]? As it is written: 'and Aaron returned to him,' etc. — and this verse speaks of Moses' descent from the mountain on the Day of Atonement, and in his hand were all the commandments given at Sinai. He further explained: and what did he see to say here — that is, what did Moses our master see to say this expression of 'the heads of the tribes, to the children of Israel' here, in the pericope of vows — in order to learn from it the other commandments? It would have been possible to say, 'and Moses spoke to the children of Israel: a man who vows a vow,' etc., and to say this expression of 'the heads of the tribes, to the children of Israel' regarding a different commandment, and from it to learn all the other commandments as well as the pericope of vows. Rather, [it is] to teach that annulment of vows [is performed] by a single expert from among the heads of the tribes, and by three laymen from 'to the children of Israel.' As was taught there: Aaron and his sons and all Israel in the pericope of vows — for what halakhah? Rav Aha bar Ya'akov said: to validate three laymen. But 'the heads of the tribes' is written! Rav Hisda said, Rabbi Yohanan [said]: by a single expert." "<b>This is the thing that YHWH commanded.</b> This thing — it is not specified where it was said to Moses. And so several prophecies, such as 'כה אמר ה׳' in the plague of locusts, and such as 'כה אמר ה׳' at midnight, and such as 'each man place his sword upon his thigh' regarding the calf — and many other prophets prophesied with 'כה אמר ה׳' and we do not find where it was said. And of this it is said: 'מקים דבר עבדו' (fulfilling the word of His servant)."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:20.909700734Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}